{"agent_id":"pp3g-2UpG-ac-3-auditor-assesses-the-overall-test-pipeline-fba1","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T00:04:42.256824397Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5e4e2b20-46ae-4b14-8bfc-c0d545707a88","comment_uuid":"88cfab03-7ced-4baf-b51e-51301c13d5bb","author":"pp3g-2UpG-ac-3-auditor-assesses-the-overall-test-pipeline-fba1","content":"Bash sandbox denies git/ls/cat despite agent config allowing them; only crosslink commands execute. KICKOFF.md 'Always allowed' list is therefore inaccurate in this environment. Worked around with crosslink CLI + filesystem tools.","created_at":"2026-08-01T00:04:42.249657791Z","kind":"intervention","trigger_type":"tool_blocked","intervention_context":"Attempted git status/log/branch, ls, cat for pipeline audit","driver_key_fingerprint":"SHA256:zGzmtgnoZhXU4eO6KSQsgBUaiDEkB/tJTAYgLkcxm+w","signed_by":"SHA256:pJDUfK4XpQphb4FKiqCSLrNKEeVmDBxt9U9n3rJTNTA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgEllOpZ4MdKjlFtOq+Om/22HVj74pMVu3qKm0dsulLt4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAY5H6VjjElmi71GoaQA4V4JAK/ABS+ytciO6t/lfJ//QBDx8p11tVc0Ulysaz4wWkzTUmw1lmJ0LiCYwUL7QBBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pJDUfK4XpQphb4FKiqCSLrNKEeVmDBxt9U9n3rJTNTA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgEllOpZ4MdKjlFtOq+Om/22HVj74pMVu3qKm0dsulLt4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH63pz/C2osGUHwMh627xLlQ4BBlA/3dmkry0c4AF2SUiHaiRi/S+vksyEmIN1BwC4FtTzlF932zINY06URrig0="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-2UpG-ac-3-auditor-assesses-the-overall-test-pipeline-fba1","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T00:08:49.856580095Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"5e4e2b20-46ae-4b14-8bfc-c0d545707a88","comment_uuid":"31ab901c-269f-4d10-a779-c7abccd30340","author":"pp3g-2UpG-ac-3-auditor-assesses-the-overall-test-pipeline-fba1","content":"## Audit Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS\n\n**Scope**: Overall test pipeline — the multi-agent Builder → Reviewer → Auditor pipeline run via crosslink kickoff in isolated worktrees (current cycle #106 → #107 → #108; parent swarm test #78; prior cycles #65–#68, #71–#74). The pipeline's objective — a full 3-phase run completing end-to-end — has still not been achieved cleanly; this is the first run in which the auditor phase is completing at all (via workarounds).\n\n**Headline finding**: The read-only agent sandbox denies commands that the agent definitions, hook-config, and KICKOFF.md all declare allowed (git status/log/diff/branch, ls, cat, echo, pwd all denied; only 'crosslink *' executes). This is a harness permission-enforcement defect, NOT a model-capability issue. It disabled the git-based evidence path, caused the three earlier AC-3 attempts on #108 to fail, and was misattributed in #78.\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n\n- [OK] — Role separation is structurally sound: builder builds, reviewer reviews, auditor audits; read-only roles enforce edit: deny (.opencode/agents/auditor.md l.9, reviewer.md l.9). This cycle is the first where roles actually matched their definitions (prior cycle #71/#73/#74 had AC-2/AC-3 implement documents instead of reviewing/auditing).\n- [OK] — Worktree isolation and per-phase agent type + model config work (AC-1/AC-2/AC-4 PASS evidence in #78, 2026-07-31 23:27).\n- [OK] — Crosslink integration works: typed comments, locks, sessions, interventions, sync.\n- [CONCERN] — Sandbox permission enforcement contradicts documented config. auditor.md/reviewer.md l.10-12 declare git */ls */cat * allow; hook-config.json allowed_bash_prefixes includes git status etc.; KICKOFF.md lists git status/diff/log/show/branch as Always allowed. Observed enforcement denies ALL of these (only crosslink * passes; even git --version passes while git status is rejected). The denial cites exactly these rules, so the matcher contradicts its own config. Verified directly on #108 (00:04 intervention) and reported for north-mini-code-free in #78.\n- [CONCERN] — Cross-worktree artifact flow is sidestepped, not fixed. AC-1's test-output.txt lives in the builder's worktree; AC-2/AC-3 tasks were redesigned as self-contained checks, so no downstream phase reads the builder artifact. The pipeline no longer exercises the artifact-handoff path that failed in the prior audit (#68 R1). It validates three independent agents, not a 3-phase flow with handoff.\n- [CONCERN] — No dependency encoding. #106/#107/#108 have empty blocked_by/blocking/related and no links to parent #78. Phase ordering is unenforced.\n- [CONCERN] — Findings-persistence references are dangling. auditor.md l.76/82 and reviewer.md l.74 link to findings/audit-findings.md, findings/audit-findings-template.md, findings/review-findings.md — none exist on this branch (findings/ contains only README.md + beds24 evidence). The #73/#74 deliverables were never merged to main; the documented observation→finding consolidation path cannot execute as written.\n\n### Process Assessment\n\n- [OK] — Comment kind discipline improved: #107 posted a structured observation (PASS with file path, line range, content evidence) + handoff; #106 used plan/handoff; my tool_blocked intervention on #108 appears in the trail (crosslink workflow trail 108).\n- [CONCERN] — #106 lacks the required result comment (tracking-normal.md: plan + result minimum); only plan + handoff.\n- [CONCERN] — Retry-without-context on #108: three identical plan comments (23:01/23:14/23:18) from failed attempts with no failure record on the issue itself; failures documented only on #78 (23:27). A retried issue should carry its own failure history.\n- [CONCERN] — Misattribution in #78: 'Model-capability finding (sandbox tool discipline), NOT a pipeline defect' is contradicted by this run — a different model hit the identical deterministic denials. The sandbox drift is a pipeline defect; model discipline is secondary. Misattribution delays the harness fix and risks repeating ~31-minute failed runs.\n- [CONCERN] — Completed-but-not-closed: #65–#68, #71–#74, #106–#108 remain open after handoff (prior audit R3 not addressed); ~100 open issues, many identical test artifacts (#33–#36, #81–#93, #96–#97).\n- [CONCERN] — Stale locks persist: 8 locks claimed 07-24/07-30 by driver identity OL2r (crosslink locks list); stale_lock_timeout_minutes 60; auto_steal_stale_locks false; sentinel disabled (prior audit R4 not addressed).\n- [CONCERN] — Documentation drift in pipeline tooling: KICKOFF.md, .crosslink/rules/global.md l.152/163, .opencode/agents/builder.md l.50, and .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts l.686/698/740 instruct 'crosslink intervene' — the top-level command does not exist in the installed binary (correct form: crosslink issue intervene). Hit directly this run.\n- [CONCERN] — Hooks not deployed: crosslink workflow diff reports .claude/hooks/{prompt-guard,post-edit-check,session-start,pre-web-check,work-check,heartbeat}.py missing. Absent heartbeat hook plausibly contributes to stale-lock accumulation and invisible agent failures.\n- [OK] — Incident transparency: #78 documents the swarm-reset DB wipe (issues #5–#105) and compact recovery.\n- [OK] — #107 reviewer performed genuine verification (quoted KICKOFF.md content) rather than fabricating — a notable improvement over prior cycles.\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n\n| Risk | Impact | Recommended mitigation |\n|---|---|---|\n| Sandbox enforcement contradicts documented permissions | Read-only roles lose git evidence; AC-3 fails repeatedly; root causes misattributed to models | Align matcher/config with agent definitions + KICKOFF.md, or intentionally deny bash and update configs so agents use filesystem tools |\n| Stale locks accumulate (driver-held, no auto-steal, sentinel off) | Issues appear locked forever; abandoned work blocks claims | Enable auto_steal_stale_locks or sentinel; release driver locks after kickoff completion |\n| No dependency encoding across phases | Phase order unenforced; traceability to parent run lost | Link phases with blocked_by; relate all to parent #78 |\n| Completed-not-closed pattern | Tracker unreliable for triage; test-issue noise | Add close step (+ --no-changelog for test issues) to kickoff final steps; archive stale test issues |\n| Dangling findings-persistence links | Observation→finding consolidation broken as documented | Merge #73/#74 findings docs to main or update agent definitions |\n| Retry-without-context | Duplicate plans; next agent loses failure context | Document failure cause on retried issue or use a fresh issue per attempt |\n| Premature end-to-end PASS claim (#78) | False confidence in pipeline reliability | Re-run full 3-phase after sandbox fix; verify before declaring PASS |\n\n### Recommendations\n\n1. **Fix read-only sandbox permission enforcement** — High. Align enforcement with .opencode/agents/*.md + hook-config allowed_bash_prefixes, OR intentionally deny bash and update all configs/docs so agents use filesystem tools. Evidence: deterministic denials despite explicit allows; 3 failed AC-3 attempts; misattribution in #78.\n2. **Correct the #78 root-cause record** — High. Amend the AC-3 failure entry to reflect the permission-enforcement defect (model discipline secondary) so the harness fix is scheduled.\n3. **Encode phase dependencies** — High. crosslink issue block 107 106 / block 108 107; relate all to #78.\n4. **Enable stale-lock cleanup** — High. auto_steal_stale_locks true or periodic steal for >60-min locks; release OL2r-held locks on completed kickoff runs.\n5. **Close completed issues with --no-changelog** — Medium. Add to kickoff final steps; close/archive stale test issues.\n6. **Resolve findings-persistence links** — Medium. Merge findings docs from #73/#74, or trim dangling references in agent definitions.\n7. **Standardize retry handoff** — Medium. On relaunch, post a plan comment noting prior attempts and failure cause.\n8. **Fix crosslink intervene references** — Low. Update KICKOFF.md template, rules/global.md, builder.md, crosslink-guard.ts to crosslink issue intervene.\n9. **Require result comment before handoff** — Low. Align kickoff template with tracking-normal.md.\n\n### Evidence Summary\n\n- #106: plan + handoff only (no result), open. #107: observation PASS + handoff, open. #108: 3 duplicate plans (23:01/23:14/23:18) + my tool_blocked intervention, open.\n- #78 result (23:27): AC-1/AC-2/AC-4 PASS; AC-3 failed 3x with north-mini-code-free; 'NOT a pipeline defect' claim contradicted by this run.\n- crosslink locks list: 8 stale locks (OL2r, 07-24/07-30), timeout 60 min, auto-steal false.\n- .opencode/agents/auditor.md l.10-12, reviewer.md l.10-12: git */ls */cat * allow; observed: all denied.\n- findings/ lacks audit-findings.md, audit-findings-template.md, review-findings.md, review-findings-template.md.\n- crosslink workflow diff: hooks missing; hook-config 102 lines customized.\n- KICKOFF.md 'Always allowed' list false in practice; 'crosslink intervene' command nonexistent (crosslink issue intervene correct).","created_at":"2026-08-01T00:08:49.850550998Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:pJDUfK4XpQphb4FKiqCSLrNKEeVmDBxt9U9n3rJTNTA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgEllOpZ4MdKjlFtOq+Om/22HVj74pMVu3qKm0dsulLt4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABApQ8bQTkj5bFwAl3xian1Q/nhJpa+2EkHT1Ud5deH5DfaRVreFDxODlpet/XDIbrL6u3/+fgFJvETQNJ62IDzCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:pJDUfK4XpQphb4FKiqCSLrNKEeVmDBxt9U9n3rJTNTA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgEllOpZ4MdKjlFtOq+Om/22HVj74pMVu3qKm0dsulLt4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFFmDxWFjgldoLLBt7RdX60aDZvmeYE5eGqrikjYYICRBHcOqc5Fd8t05fF20jBrc7Y/RvXRz68v7IRtzv1ctAw="}
